    "M15-MASTER-BLOCK-DISPATCH-ORACLE-VERIFICATION.json"
  ],
  "implementation": "A separate ephemeral reaction request admits bare defenders with base HTH>=Journeyman against weapon contacts while retaining full Health damage and Block-derived Fatigue. The ordinary caller uses the original general sound fallback below Journeyman Block; at/above that rank actual original block palette uses two Hand layers. Advanced zero absorption enters blocked Counter-first dispatch and skips general-hit force. No schema/default change.",
  "unit_coverage": [
    "54 Player/NPC defender contexts: base HTH49/50/74/75/99/100 plus modified-vs-base thresholds, Block5/25/50, full damage16, zero absorption, Block-based costs and original sound-rank split; query is read only",
    "Owned NPC bare defense: Counter miss then inclusive Master disarm, one drop, full damage, explicit H2H reactions and exact binary restoration",
    "Ordinary selected-target dispatcher with real actor collision bodies: full damage, general hit sound layers, no general-hit force, one Counter roll and binary restoration; headless fixture does not create renderer resources"
  ],
  "failures_retained": [
    "normal01: owned fixture faced away, producing unblocked damage and no Recoil request. SAN01 deliberately interrupted on known incomplete version; not a sanitizer result.",
    "normal02/SAN02: compile rejection of mutation through const position accessor, corrected with RefData.setPosition.",
    "normal03:1844 passed/1 failed; owned loose drop correctly rejected residual7.25 charge on a weapon whose enchantment had been cleared. Numeric54-context and ordinary selected-target tests passed.",
    "SAN03 intentionally interrupted for known fixture charge correction (child-9), not a sanitizer pass or fault diagnosis.",
    "Both04 full suites include charge sentinel-1 and pass1845 tests/125 suites. Prior reports remain in their original evidence directories."
  ],
